{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794857784871787285,"compiled_state":{"alias":"breezy-hogged-mastiff","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"21821d7554b9ed3bb27577e09318033bb9cf553d6d731e4bab52a8250eddaf5a","event_uuid":"d9494472-8f84-4020-9a00-6dfa19896b43","position":{"commit_sha":"e7793891306ff2555b652e3076e20d5d81a770b8","position":"1794857692045684963-d9494472-8f84-4020-9a00-6dfa19896b43"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"27386c7fe1ecf7cb8998fca90cfd828c5eab40e787171c906b7509ea54003f7d","event_uuid":"04cb20bd-83d4-4e1c-818f-cf29fa19993c","position":{"commit_sha":"8857639c3e35373f52af5e6c5423daef7285494a","position":"1794857784871787284-04cb20bd-83d4-4e1c-818f-cf29fa19993c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794857692045684963,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"04cb20bd-83d4-4e1c-818f-cf29fa19993c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. This bug owns that file: 242 tests in 100 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nThese failed on Windows with assertion-level messages that match none of the signatures used for the other classes (MAX_PATH, POSIX shell, text encoding, POSIX permissions, path separators, POSIX APIs, nested-pytest plugins, literal `/tmp`, file locks). Largest modules: `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py` (12), `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py` (10), `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py` (8), `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` (8), `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` (7), `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py` (7). Some may be downstream of the larger classes (for example a git or path failure surfacing as an assertion).\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the larger class bugs land, re-measure: read each remaining failure's full traceback in a fresh sweep log. Move an entry into the matching class file (and its bug) when the cause matches; group the residue by root cause and fix it, filing a new class bug linked `discovered_from` this one where a group is large.\n\n## Scope\n\nTest or product code for the residue, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args` (remove each fixed or reclassified line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each remaining entry's root cause is recorded on this ticket or the class bug it moved to.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `unclassified.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix, or now sits in another class file (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 242 failures not yet root-caused into a defect class","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d9494472-8f84-4020-9a00-6dfa19896b43","04cb20bd-83d4-4e1c-818f-cf29fa19993c"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794857784871787285,"uuid":"8aaf32a9-f52f-48ee-970b-1813dcd6ea59"}
